From: Camera firmware maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] http: reject encoded NUL request targets and query values

Reject ambiguous NUL-bearing HTTP request targets before routing or generic
callbacks, and reject decoded NUL in query values stored as C strings.
Keep evhttp_uridecode's documented binary behavior, including size_out=NULL.
This is a local HTTP-boundary mitigation of the remaining URI condition in
CVE-2026-63385, not a change to arbitrary callers of the binary decoder.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local hardening at HTTP string boundaries]
Reference: https://github.com/libevent/libevent/security/advisories/GHSA-jcwh-pvf2-73p2

--- a/http.c
+++ b/http.c
@@ -1754,6 +1754,12 @@
 	*version = '\0';
 	version++;
 
+	/* HTTP request targets become C strings in routing and applications.
+	 * Reject encoded NUL before dispatch, while keeping the general-purpose
+	 * binary percent-decoding API unchanged. */
+	if (strstr(uri, "%00") != NULL)
+		return -1;
+
 	method_len = (uri - method) - 1;
 	type       = EVHTTP_REQ_UNKNOWN_;
 
@@ -3461,8 +3467,13 @@
 			event_warn("%s: mm_malloc", __func__);
 			goto error;
 		}
-		evhttp_decode_uri_internal(value, strlen(value),
+		err = evhttp_decode_uri_internal(value, strlen(value),
 		    decoded_value, 1 /*always_decode_plus*/);
+		/* Header values cannot represent embedded NUL bytes. */
+		if (memchr(decoded_value, '\0', (size_t)err) != NULL) {
+			mm_free(decoded_value);
+			goto error;
+		}
 		event_debug(("Query Param: %s -> %s\n", key, decoded_value));
 		err = evhttp_add_header_internal(headers, key, decoded_value);
 		mm_free(decoded_value);
